{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>מי</b> — Rabbi Moses said: The meaning is that all his desire is in heaven, for he is with the angels, as if he said: All that is mine is in heaven and with You; I have no desire on earth. Rabbi Judah HaLevi [said of] מ\"כ: \"Who is it that I seek? He is in heaven,\" in the manner of: מי לך כל המחנה הזה אשר פגשתי (Genesis 33:8). According to the opinion of the Gaon [Saadia]: that the word זולתך is lacking after בשמים. And according to my opinion: that he has no desire in heaven or on earth after the loss of his body; therefore, \"after Him.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {0 "The abbreviation מ\"כ is unresolved; rendered here as introducing Rabbi Judah HaLevi's reading of the phrase מי כמוך, but the expansion is uncertain. The final clause 'על כן אחריו' is terse and the antecedent of 'his body' is ambiguous; translated hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:22.020079539Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}